    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_1f66455f",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image features a man in a plaid shirt pointing aggressively, set against a red backdrop with event logos. The text overlay reads: 'i don't need you to tell me how fuckin good my memes are... i get reported all the fuckin time.' The overall intent is to express frustration or defensiveness about being frequently flagged or reported for content, likely memes, on social media platforms. The tone is confrontational and uses profanity to convey irritation. There is no evidence of toxicity targeting specific protected groups (race, gender, religion, etc.), nor does it contain abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propagandistic content. The intent is self-referential and humorous, using the visual of an angry or dismissive gesture to amplify the textual message about online moderation and perceived unfairness in content reporting. The analogical mapping is between the man's aggressive pointing gesture and the frustration expressed in the text, suggesting he is 'pointing the finger' at the system or audience responsible for the reports.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_bab643f8"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
